00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:09.430
another study came out from a belgian research
group at the end of march and they found that

00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:14.830
benzophenone increased after octocrylene sunscreens
were kept at high temperatures so again i

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:18.890
don't think the experiment part of this study
was wrong but if you compare the two papers

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:23.510
you can see how differently the two papers
contextualize their findings the other paper

00:17:23.510 --> 00:17:28.481
mentions that benzophenone is a potential
endocrine disruptor and carcinogen but it

00:17:28.481 --> 00:17:30.440
really highlights the potential part

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:34.070
there are a bunch of other things i haven't
mentioned that to me also seem like pretty

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:39.920
big red flags for example dinardo's public
email address for a while was chemicalsrtoxic@gmail.com

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:45.650
downs' lab runs a program that's a lot like
the ewg approved label where they'll certify

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:48.330
that your sunscreens are reef safe for a fee

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:53.500
last minute edit: last week one of the authors
from the lab affiliated with pierre fabre

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:58.430
commented on my coral reef post about adding
info on octocrylene being bad I'm not sure

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:04.090
why he's reaching out to someone he called
a "propaganda source" seems kinda sus

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:09.460
so what are the takeaways from this with octocrylene
and benzophenone the vast majority of scientists

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:13.590
don't think that benzophenone is as bad as
the paper makes it out to be but the amount

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:18.060
can get higher than expected although it is
still within the margin of safety for oral

00:18:18.060 --> 00:18:22.160
exposure so hopefully there'll be a bit more
research on how benzophenone affects humans

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:27.640
when we put it on our skin and sunscreen formulators
will focus on ways of stabilizing octocrylene

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:33.190
in the meantime as many skincare experts have
said it's probably still safe to use octocrylene

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:37.770
sunscreens as long as you're not allergic
to them but it's safest to not use sunscreens

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:42.530
after their used by date and not expose them
to high temperatures which you were hopefully

00:18:42.530 --> 00:18:43.530
doing anyway

00:18:43.530 --> 00:18:48.090
the wider takeaway is that you can't trust
everything you read just because it's in a

00:18:48.090 --> 00:18:52.910
peer-reviewed paper this paper had five authors
who all apparently signed off on this and

00:18:52.910 --> 00:18:57.000
there were four anonymous reviewers as well
stuff slips through peer review all the time

00:18:57.000 --> 00:19:01.920
especially when it's commentary around the
relevance of the research that part isn't

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:05.870
checked anywhere near as thoroughly as the
actual experimental part of the paper

